# Served by Cloudflare Workers static assets (this file is copied into
# .open-next/assets by the build). Hashed Next chunks and fonts are immutable
# by construction — a changed file gets a new hash — so browsers may cache
# them for a year instead of revalidating every chunk on every visit
# (launch review 2026-07-31).

# Security headers, added 2026-08-04. next.config.js headers() only decorate
# responses the OpenNext worker renders; Workers Assets serves these files
# ahead of the worker, so they previously shipped with no HSTS, no nosniff and
# no framing rules. /sw.js was the sharpest edge — a service worker is the most
# powerful script on the origin and it was the one response with neither MIME
# enforcement nor transport pinning. Rules cascade, so the per-path
# Cache-Control blocks below still apply.
# Permissions-Policy and CSP added 2026-08-06 to match next.config.js. The
# worker-rendered routes had both; these responses had neither, so /sw.js —
# the most powerful script on the origin — was the one script the origin
# served with no CSP at all.
#
# This CSP is deliberately TIGHTER than the rendered-route policy and is not
# a copy of it. These paths serve static assets, not the app: no inline
# script is involved, so there is no 'unsafe-inline' here (the rendered-route
# policy only carries it for Cloudflare's injected inline script — see
# docs/SECURITY.md), and no Supabase origin, because nothing served from here
# talks to Supabase. sw.js is same-origin only by construction: its fetch
# handler returns early on `url.origin !== self.location.origin`, so
# default-src 'self' cannot break it.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'

/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/favicon.ico
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/favicon.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/apple-touch-icon.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/og.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

# The service worker must never be cached long — a stale worker pins users to
# a stale app. Browsers bypass HTTP cache for SW updates within 24h anyway;
# no-cache makes every check hit the network.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/manifest.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/icon-192.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/icon-512.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
